&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Earth Observations Webinar Series&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Earth Observations: Conversations with Lamont Scientists&lt;/em&gt; webinar series, launched to commemorate Lamont-Doherty Earth Observatory&amp;rsquo;s 75th anniversary, aims to engage our&amp;nbsp;global community of alumni, supporters, and colleagues through informative virtual discussions. This year&amp;rsquo;s lineup includes four programs featuring presentations by Lamont researchers, each followed by an open Q&amp;amp;A session with the audience.&amp;nbsp;We invite you to join these conversations and engage with the exciting research and discoveries unfolding at Lamont-Doherty.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Teachers&amp;rsquo; Lounges&lt;/strong&gt; are a series of informal discussions for graduate students and postdocs about teaching practices and the culture of learning at Columbia. Our conversations often introduce participants to related educational models, research, and theory, and invite dialogue about their pertinence to day to day teaching.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2026&amp;ndash;2027, Teachers&amp;#39; Lounge&amp;nbsp;is exploring &lt;strong&gt;What Games Know about Learning&lt;/strong&gt;. In this&amp;nbsp;three-part series, participants will discuss how to leverage game design principles to create more engaging, motivating, and student-centered learning experiences, regardless of discipline. Join us for one or all of the sessions to become part of a collaborative teaching and learning community. No gaming background is needed!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this second&amp;nbsp;session, &lt;strong&gt;Level Up: Applying the Mechanics of Gaming to Learning&lt;/strong&gt;, participants will go deeper into the mechanics of gaming that matter most for learning: feedback, progression, agency, and failure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This session is in-person and will be facilitated by &lt;a href="https://ctl.columbia.edu/about/team/kalender/" target="_blank"&gt;Yasemin Kalender&lt;/a&gt; from the Center for Teaching and Learning. Vegetarian/vegan lunch&amp;nbsp;will be available to registered participants.&lt;/p&gt;
